"secId":"qii3-section4",
"content":"VIDEO The Environmental Challenge and Opportunity 3 min watch Infrastructure's Environmental Footprint Infrastructure shapes environmental outcomes for generations. Without intentional action, projects can: Lock in carbon-intensive pathways through decisions made at the planning and design stages, with emissions persisting across decades of operation. Bypass critical environmental safeguards, resulting in irreversible damage to ecosystems, water systems, and air quality. Overlook nature-based alternatives that could deliver services while regenerating natural capital and benefiting local communities."
